As a data analyst, you have been tasked with retrieving and analyzing basketball player stats. Using C# code, you must pull the stats of the player who scored the highest points per game in a particular season.
To do this, you can use the following code:
using System.Net;
using System.IO;
int season = 2021; // enter the desired season here
string url = "https://stats.nba.com/stats/leagueleaders?LeagueID=00&PerMode=PerGame&Scope=S&Season=" + season + "&SeasonType=Regular+Season&StatCategory=PTS";
WebRequest request = WebRequest.Create(url);
WebResponse response = request.GetResponse();
Stream data = response.GetResponseStream();
StreamReader reader = new StreamReader(data);
string responseFromServer = reader.ReadToEnd();
// Parse the JSON response to extract the desired stats
// Example: points per game for the player with the highest PPG in the season
double highestPPG = double.Parse(responseFromServer["resultSet"]["rowSet"][0][22].ToString());
Your task is to modify this code to also retrieve the player's rebounds per game (RPG) and assists per game (APG), and then calculate their total contribution (TC) as follows: TC = PPG + (RPG x 1.2) + (APG x 1.5).
Your final output should be the name of the player who had the highest total contribution in the desired season. Good luck!

answer:
Here is the modified code to retrieve the player's stats and calculate their total contribution:
using System;
using System.Net;
using System.IO;
using Newtonsoft.Json.Linq;
int season = 2021; // enter the desired season here
string url = "https://stats.nba.com/stats/leagueleaders?LeagueID=00&PerMode=PerGame&Scope=S&Season=" + season + "&SeasonType=Regular+Season&StatCategory=PTS";
WebRequest request = WebRequest.Create(url);
WebResponse response = request.GetResponse();
Stream data = response.GetResponseStream();
StreamReader reader = new StreamReader(data);
string responseFromServer = reader.ReadToEnd();
// Parse the JSON response to extract the desired stats
JObject json = JObject.Parse(responseFromServer);
JArray rowSet = (JArray)json["resultSet"]["rowSet"];
double highestTC = 0;
string playerName = "";
foreach (JToken row in rowSet)
{
    double PPG = double.Parse(row[22].ToString());
    double RPG = double.Parse(row[18].ToString());
    double APG = double.Parse(row[19].ToString());
    double TC = PPG + (RPG * 1.2) + (APG * 1.5);
    if (TC > highestTC)
    {
        highestTC = TC;
        playerName = row[2].ToString();
    }
}
Console.WriteLine("The player with the highest total contribution in the {0} season is {1} with a total contribution of {2}", season, playerName, highestTC);
Note that the code uses the Newtonsoft.Json library to parse the JSON response. You can install this library using NuGet package manager.

