Here's the modified Scala code that calculates the sum of all odd numbers from the starting number to the ending number using a recursive function:

```scala
def sumOfOddNumbers(start: Int = 1, end: Int): Int = {
  if (end < start) {
    0
  } else if (start % 2 == 0) {
    sumOfOddNumbers(start + 1, end)
  } else {
    start + sumOfOddNumbers(start + 2, end)
  }
}

// example usage
val result = sumOfOddNumbers(1, 10) // returns 25
println(result) // prints 25 to the console
```

