The reason behind this behavior is that the `document.querySelector` method is used to select elements in the DOM, and Aura Components and LWCs use different shadow DOM implementations. In Aura, the components use the Shadow DOM, which creates a separate DOM tree that is not accessible via the regular DOM selectors. On the other hand, LWCs use the Light DOM, which is similar to the regular DOM tree.

Since `document.querySelector` is only able to select elements in the regular DOM tree and not in the Shadow DOM tree, it is not able to find the LWC element. However, since the LWC is using the Light DOM, the element is available via the regular DOM.

To overcome this issue, you can use the `this.template.querySelector` method in the Aura component to target the LWC element. This method will search for the element within the Aura component's DOM tree and is able to find elements in both the Shadow and Light DOM.

Here's an example of how to use `this.template.querySelector` to target the child button element in the LWC component from an Aura component:

```
