To limit the maximum length of a field in bytes to a specific number of bytes, while taking into account the presence of Unicode characters within the string, you can use the $substrCP operator. This operator extracts a substring from a string based on the number of Unicode code points, rather than the number of bytes. By specifying the maximum number of code points allowed in the substring, you can limit the maximum length of the field. 

