To ensure an image is centered when uploaded to a GitHub repository and is responsive across multiple devices, the following steps can be taken:

1. Create a new repository on GitHub and navigate to the "Settings" tab.
2. Scroll down to the "GitHub Pages" section and select a theme for your website. This will create a default `index.html` file in your repository, which you can edit later.
3. Navigate to the "Upload files" button and upload your image. Make sure the file name is in all lowercase and does not contain any spaces or special characters. GitHub will automatically convert your image to a URL.
4. Open the `index.html` file and add the following code:

```html
<div class="image-container">
  <img src="image-url-here" alt="Image description">
</div>
```

5. In the CSS section of your `index.html` file, add the following code:

```css
.image-container {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: center;
  align-items: center;
  height: 100vh;
}

img {
  max-width: 100%;
  height: auto;
}
```

6. Save and commit your changes to the repository.
7. Test the responsiveness of the image by opening your website on different devices or by resizing your browser window.

The above steps ensure that your image is centered and responsive on different devices. The `display: flex;` property in the `.image-container` class aligns the image both vertically and horizontally, while the `max-width: 100%;` property in the `img` class ensures that the image scales down proportionally to fit the container on smaller devices.

