Great question! There are several libraries available for generating PDFs in nodejs, but my personal favorite is `pdfkit`. Here's an example of how to use it to generate a PDF from an HTML template:

```javascript
const PDFDocument = require('pdfkit');
const fs = require('fs');
const htmlToPdf = require('html-pdf');

// Assume you have your invoice data and HTML template already
const invoiceData = {...};
const invoiceTemplate = fs.readFileSync('path/to/invoice_template.html', 'utf8');

// Create a new PDF document
const doc = new PDFDocument();

// Pipe the PDF document to a write stream
const writeStream = fs.createWriteStream('path/to/invoice.pdf');
doc.pipe(writeStream);

// Convert the HTML template to a PDF
htmlToPdf.create(invoiceTemplate).toBuffer((err, buffer) => {
  if (err) throw err;

  // Embed the PDF in the new document
  const pdf = new PDFDocument({ bufferPages: true });
  pdf.pipe(doc);
  pdf.end(buffer);

  // Add the invoice data to the document
  doc.text(JSON.stringify(invoiceData));

  // End the document
  doc.end();
});
```

This code creates a new `PDFDocument` and pipes it to a write stream, then converts the HTML template to a PDF using the `html-pdf` library and embeds it in the document using `pdfkit`. Finally, it adds the invoice data as text to the document and ends it.

